    "## Model Compilation\n",
    "\n",
    "The BiLSTM model was compiled using the **Adam optimizer**, **Binary Cross-Entropy loss function**, and **Accuracy** as the evaluation metric. These choices were made based on the nature of the dataset and the binary classification problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Optimizer: Adam\n",
    "\n",
    "The Adam (Adaptive Moment Estimation) optimizer was selected because it combines the advantages of Momentum and RMSProp. It automatically adapts the learning rate for each parameter, resulting in faster convergence and more stable training. Adam is widely used in Natural Language Processing tasks due to its efficiency and robustness.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Learning Rate: 0.001\n",
    "\n",
    "A learning rate of **0.001** was chosen because it is the default and most commonly recommended value for the Adam optimizer. It provides a good balance between learning speed and training stability. Higher learning rates may cause unstable training, while lower values increase the training time without significant performance improvements for this dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Loss Function: Binary Cross-Entropy\n",
    "\n",
    "The MCQ task was converted into a binary classification problem at the **question-option pair level**. Each question was paired separately with its five answer options:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **1** → Correct option\n",
    "- **0** → Incorrect option\n",
    "\n",
    "The BiLSTM therefore learns to assign a probability to each question-option pair. The five probabilities are subsequently ranked to produce the Top-3 answer options required by the competition.\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the output layer contains a single neuron with a Sigmoid activation, Binary Cross-Entropy is appropriate for the pairwise classification objective.\n",
    "### 4. Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The model was monitored using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and AUC during training.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Accuracy** measures the proportion of correctly classified question-option pairs.\n",
    "- **Precision** measures how many predicted positive option pairs were actually correct.\n",
    "- **Recall** measures how many of the true correct option pairs were successfully identified.\n",
    "- **AUC** measures the model's ability to distinguish correct from incorrect option pairs across classification thresholds.\n",
    "\n",
    "The final **F1 score** was also calculated from validation precision and recall.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Hyperparameter | Selected Value | Justification |\n",
    "|----------------|---------------|---------------|\n",
    "| Optimizer | Adam | Fast convergence and adaptive learning rates for NLP tasks |\n",
    "| Learning Rate | 0.001 | Stable default value for Adam that balances speed and convergence |\n",
    "| Loss Function | Binary Cross-Entropy | Suitable for binary classification using Sigmoid output |\n",
    "| Evaluation Metric | Accuracy, AUC| Accuracy measures correct predictions, while AUC evaluates the model's discrimination ability across thresholds |"
