    "### Error Analysis Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "The common leakage-free validation set contained **361 MCQs**. BiLSTM produced **0 incorrect Top-1 predictions**, while DistilBERT produced **47 errors** and RAG produced **62 errors**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This corresponds to error rates of 0.00% for BiLSTM, 7.76% for DistilBERT, and 17.17% for RAG.\n",
    "\n",
    "The three models disagreed on **99 validation questions**, showing that the models do not always make the same decisions even when evaluated on the same questions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The disagreement analysis is useful for understanding the complementary behaviour of the models. In several cases, BiLSTM and DistilBERT agreed with the correct answer while RAG selected a different option. This indicates that retrieved context and semantic reranking do not always lead to the correct final answer.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, BiLSTM was the strongest individual model on this validation split, while the different prediction patterns of the three models provided motivation for testing an ensemble."
